                ("p", "A base model is trained on a broad, general dataset at significant cost. Fine-tuning takes that already-trained model and runs additional training passes on a narrower dataset representative of a specific task, domain, or desired output style, adjusting the weights further rather than starting over. This is far cheaper than training from scratch because the model has already learned general language structure and broad knowledge; fine-tuning only needs to shift it toward a narrower target."),
